<h2>1. ElevenLabs — Best for Voiceover</h2>
<p>For narration, ElevenLabs is the default choice for a reason that shows up on the pricing page: 74 languages, a free tier with 10,000 credits a month, and voice cloning that starts from a one-to-two-minute sample (Professional Voice Cloning needs about 30 minutes of reference audio). The current flagship model is Eleven v4, marketed as the most emotive text-to-speech model the company has shipped, alongside Flash v2.5 for ~100ms median latency in real-time use.</p>
<p>The number that matters for budgeting is the credit rate: one character of text equals roughly one credit. So Starter's 30,000 credits is about 30 minutes of finished speech per month, and Creator's 121,000 credits is roughly two hours. A weekly 12-minute video with a light script usually fits Creator; a channel publishing twice a week should price Scale ($299/month, 1.8M credits) before committing.</p>

