<h2>5. OpusClip — Best for Volume Clipping</h2>
<p>OpusClip is the other half of the long-to-shorts market: point it at a long video or a YouTube link and it selects moments, reframes to vertical, adds animated captions and gives each clip a virality score. The score is a sorting aid, not a promise — but it does let you rank ten clips before watching any of them.</p>
<p>Free allows one clip a day with watermarked animated captions and 9:16 only. Starter is $15/month and removes the watermark, adds the virality score, YouTube auto-import and 30-day media retention. Pro is $29/month for 1:1 and 16:9, topics search, prompt-to-clip, custom fonts and API access.</p>

