<h2>6. CapCut — Best Free Editor</h2>
<p>CapCut remains the default free editor for YouTube and Shorts work: a real timeline, templates, auto-captions and export presets sized for each platform. For creators who cut a handful of videos a week, the free tier covers the job and costs nothing.</p>
<p>Paid tiers (Pro, Ultra, Teams) add AI credits, premium templates, 1 TB storage and extra AI generations, with a 7-day free Pro trial and no credit card required. One caveat that is easy to miss: CapCut quotes prices in local currency and states that displayed pricing is for reference until you sign in, so the number you see depends on region and platform.</p>

