<h2>8. Midjourney — Best Thumbnail Imagery</h2>
<p>When a thumbnail needs an image that does not exist — a dramatic composite, a stylised subject, a background that reads at 120 pixels wide — Midjourney still produces the most distinctive output, and its style-reference feature keeps a channel's thumbnails visually consistent across a series.</p>
<p>There is no free plan. Basic is $10/month (about 3.3 fast GPU hours), Standard is $30/month for 15 fast hours plus unlimited Relax generations, Pro is $60/month for Stealth mode and 30 hours, Mega is $120/month for 60 hours. Annual billing cuts roughly 20%. The unit is GPU time, not images, so batching prompts in Relax mode is what keeps the cost per usable thumbnail low.</p>

